hadiths[49]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2672","Siyar said: I was walking with Thabit al-Banani, he used to greet the children when he passed by them, then narrated the hadith that he was with Sayyidna Anas, when he passed by the children, he used to greet them, and Sayyidna Anas said that he was with the Prophet, peace be upon him, and when he passed by the children, he greeted them."
"2673","It was narrated from a woman of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, Sayyida Asma bint Yazid bin Sakin, that she was with some women whom the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by and greeted them."
"2674","Saida Aisha, the blessed wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \O Aisha! This is Jibreel"
"2675","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghafari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying. When he finished praying, I came to him, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was the first person to offer the Islamic greeting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in reply: \Aleik Salam and Rahmatullah"
"2676","Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) said: A companion came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: “Peace be upon you.” He (PBUH) replied and said: “Ten.” Then other Companions came and greeted him like this: Peace be upon you and peace be upon you. He (PBUH) also answered this and said: \Twenty.\"" Then another companion came"
"2677","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Mahajir bin Qunfuth (RA) that he greeted the Prophet (PBUH). At that time, the Prophet (PBUH) was urinating, so he did not respond to his salam, then he (PBUH) performed ablution, then responded to the salam."
"2678","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Do not go to women (alone).\"" The Companions said: \""O Messenger! Except for Hamu (i.e. exclude Hamu from it)"
"2679","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (RA) that he asked the Prophet (PBUH) about his sudden sight, and he (PBUH) said: \Turn away your sight.\"""""
"2680","Sayyidah Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the skirts of women (i.e., how much should they hang)? He said: \Keep a pillow (big).\"" Sayyida Umm Salama (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah! Then the steps will open when walking? He said: \""Then hang one hand"
"2681","The sister of Sayyiduna Huzaifa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us a sermon and said: \O women! Can you not wear silver ornaments? See: Any woman among you who wears gold ornaments and shows them (i.e. she shows her adornment to men with pride and arrogance and disrespect) will be punished because of it.\"""""
"2682","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him: A woman who wears perfume and goes out so that people can smell her fragrance is an adulteress, and every eye is an adulteress. \n Abu Asim said: Some of our Sheikhs have narrated it with authority."
"2683","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: Allah has cursed those who knead and those who knead, those who pull out hair, and those who widen cracks in their teeth for the sake of beauty, and those who change the creation of Allah. He said: What happened to you that I should not curse him whom the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed, and this is also in the Book of Allah. She said: I have read the entire Holy Quran, but I did not find what you are saying in it? Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If you had read (carefully) the Qur'an, you would have found it in it. Didn't you read: \Follow what the Messenger commands you and refrain from what he forbids you...\"" (Hashr: 7/59). He said: Yes"
"2684","Abu Aamir said: I heard from the companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, Sayyidna Abu Rihana Shimoun bin Zayd, that he used to say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to forbid ten things: \Two men sleeping together without clothes (naked)"
"2685","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, cursed the effeminate men and the women who adopted the behavior of men and said: \Evict these women and men from your homes.\"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) expelled such and such a hijra"
"2686","Zareah bin Abd al-Rahman narrated from his father Abd al-Rahman (b. Jarhad, may God be pleased with him) who was among the Companions of Safa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting near us and my thigh was open. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Cover it"
"2687","Salim bin Abi al-Jaad said: Some women from Homs (Syria) came to the service of Umm al-Momineen Sayyida Aisha (may God be pleased with her) and wanted to ask her something. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Perhaps you are one of those women who go to the bath? He replied: Yes, Sayyida Aisha (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \A woman who takes off her clothes in any place other than her husband's house has torn the veil that is between her and Allah.\"" \n Imam al-Darmi"
"2688","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \No one should take another person from his place so that he may sit there himself"
"2689","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When one of you\"" or he said: \""When a man gets up from his place (for some need) and then returns"
"2690","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Bara' that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some people of the Ansar who were sitting on the road, and he (peace be upon him) said: \If it is necessary for you to sit here"
"2691","Ibad bin Tamim narrated from his uncle Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asim Mazni (RA) that he saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) lying on a mat in the mosque and he was placing one foot over the other."
"2692","Sayyidina Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \When there are three of you"
"2693","Sayyidina Abu Burza Aslami (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was sitting in an assembly and was about to stand up, he would say: \Subhaanak Allahum...... Atubbu ilaik\"" O Allah! I do.” People said: O Messenger of Allah! At first you did not say what you say now? He said: \""This is an atonement for what was said in the assembly.\"""""
"2694","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Ayyub Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The person who sneezes will say: “Al-hamdu lillah ali kul’ halal” (thanks to God in every situation), and the listener will say in response: “Yarhamukum-Allah” (may God have mercy on you), then the person who sneezes will say. He will say: \May Allah guide you and correct you.\"""""
"2695","Sayyidina Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Two men sneezed near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) responded. You answered this one and didn't answer the other one? He said: \He said Alhamdulillah and he did not say Alhamdulillah.\"" Imam Darmi"
"2696","Ayyas bin Salama said: My father narrated the hadith, saying: A man sneezed near the Prophet. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him YarahmakAllah, and when he sneezed again, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \The servant has a cold.\"""""
"2697","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We had a sheet with images made of it, I placed it in front of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), while he was praying, so he stopped me, or said that he disliked it. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: So I cut it and made it into pillows."
"2698","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Indeed"
"2699","Sayyidina Abu Mas'ud Badri (RA) said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a Muslim spends on his family (wife and children) in the hope of reward from Allah"
"2700","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Jafar (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) would return from a journey, he would find me and Sayyidna Hasan or Sayyidna Husain (RA) standing to receive them. The narrator said: I believe that he was Sayyiduna Hasan (RA), so he (PBUH) made me ride in front of him and Sayyiduna Hasan (RA) behind him until we entered Madinah and we were riding on the same animal that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was riding on."
"2701","On the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid al-Khatami, who was the governor of Kufa, he said: We went to the house of Qays bin Saad bin Ubadah, the muezzin gave the call to prayer, we said to Qays: Get up and lead us in prayer. He replied that I cannot lead the prayer to a nation of which I am not rich. On hearing this, a person who was not of low status - his name was Abdullah bin Hanzala bin al-Ghasil - said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The master has more right to his ride"
"2702","Muhammad bin Hamzah bin Amr Aslami said and his father Sayyiduna Hamzah was in the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: I heard from my father, he used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is a devil on the hump of every camel, so when you are riding a camel, mention the name of Allah (i.e. say Bismillah) and do not reduce your needs.”"
"2703","On the authority of Sahl bin Anas, he narrated from his father who was among the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Ride these animals until they are tired and injured"
"2704","Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Abdullah bin Saleh informed us on the authority of Layth, but his narration is somewhat different from that of Shababa bin Sawar."
"2705","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Journey is a part of punishment"
"2706","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) said: A companion came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said: O Prophet of Allah! I plan to travel? He (peace be upon him) said: \When?\"" He said: Tomorrow"
"2707","Abdullah bin Sarjis said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make this supplication while traveling: \O Allah"
"2708","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go on a journey and sit on a horse, he would say Allahu Akbar three times and then say this supplication: \Glory be to Him Who has made this ride tame for us"
"2709","Narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: When we used to climb high, we used to say Allahu Akbar and when we came down, we used to say Subhan Allah."
"2710","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyida Umm Habiba (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \The angels do not stay with the caravan in which there is a bell.\"""""
"2711","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The angels do not stay with those travelers who have a dog or a bell with them.\"""""
"2712","It was narrated from Imran bin Hussain (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) was on a journey when he heard someone cursing and said: \What is this?\"" People said that such and such a woman has cursed her ride. He said: \""Take off the goods from him because he has been cursed.\"" So people have taken things from him. Sayyidna Imran (RA) said: As if I was looking at her"
"2713","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \A woman should not travel for three days or more than three days without her father"
"2714","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If people knew the evil of solitude"
"2715","Saida Khula bint Hakeem, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When someone lands in a place (on a journey) and says: ``Awudhu bikalimat-i-Allah-i-al-Tammamat-i min-shar'' ma-khalak\"" then nothing in that destination will harm him until he moves from that place.'' \n Translated supplication: I seek refuge with the complete words of Allah from the evil of what He has created."""
"2716","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) landed at a place on a journey, he would not leave that place until he had prayed two rak'ahs, or he had left that place after praying two rak'ahs. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Uthman bin Saad is weak in his chain of transmission."
"2717","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that when the Prophet (PBUH) returned from his journey, he used to make this supplication: \Ibûn in shaa'Allah......Hamidun\"" means we who return"
"2718","(Marfu' Hadith) Abu al-Walid informed us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Bara' ibn 'Azib saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded a man, when he takes his place in bed (to sleep), to say: ""O Allah, I have submitted my soul to You, and I have turned my face to You, and I have entrusted my affair to You, and I have sought refuge with You, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed, and Your Prophet whom You sent. If he dies, he dies upon the Fitrah (natural monotheism)."""
"2719","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may God be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When one of you lies down on a bed"
"2720","Ameerul Momineen Sayyidna Ali bin Abi Talib (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) came to us until he placed his (blessed) foot between me and Sayyida Fatima (RA) and taught us that when we go to bed, say \Subhan Allah\"" 33 times"
